  "title": "Jacobi Elliptic — reference 1",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "Jacobi Elliptic — reference 1",
    "name_source": "document",
    "description": "Relier les contrôles aux ports nommés, puis lancer Run. Les types et valeurs sont explicites; sélectionner la fiche n'exécute rien.\nEntrées : argument (f64) = 0.0; parameter (f64) = 0.0.\nRésultats attendus : cn (f64) = 1.0; dn (f64) = 1.0; sn (f64) = 0.0; amplitude (f64) = 0.0.\n\nEvaluates Jacobi cn, dn, sn and continuous amplitude phi for real x and parameter m=k (not k squared and not the modulus).\n\nMode: execution. Profile: studio-draft. Capability: windows-x64; LLVM 22.1.7; exact declared scalar signature.\nExpected:\noutput-cn (f64) = 1.0\noutput-dn (f64) = 1.0\noutput-sn (f64) = 0.0\noutput-amplitude (f64) = 0.0\n",
    "author": "",
    "automatic_versioning": false,
    "program_version": "0.0.0.0",
    "tags": ["numeric-math", "typed-values", "independent-oracle", "example"],
    "documentation_uri": ""
  },
